<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Downloader on Saitech</title><link>https://saiphe.com/tags/downloader/</link><description>Recent content in Downloader on Saitech</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 18 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://saiphe.com/tags/downloader/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>ytDownloader</title><link>https://saiphe.com/p/ytdownloader/</link><pubDate>Sat, 18 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://saiphe.com/p/ytdownloader/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://saiphe.com/p/ytdownloader/1.png" alt="Featured image of post ytDownloader" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;For years I was using online solutions to download music from YouTube… not anymore. This simple GUI solves all my issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can download it directly from the &lt;b&gt;&lt;a class="link" href="https://github.com/aandrew-me/ytDownloader" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Github page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;or if you’re on Arch Linux, just run this in your terminal:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;flatpak install flathub io.github.aandrew_me.ytdn
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Using it is so much easier than trying to describe it, so… go figure it out yourself 😁&lt;/p&gt;
